# Agent fleet — run the SAME pipeline with different models, side by side.
#
# Every agent shares the expensive/curated stuff: SociaVault calls and web fetches
# happen ONCE per run (credits are spent once), and all agents read the same
# igaccounts.md / websites.md / interests.yaml / memory.yaml. What differs per
# agent is the model — and therefore its database, memory, suggestions, reports,
# and cost.
#
# SETUP: copy this file to `agents.yaml` (or put it in $AGENT_STATE_DIR/config/):
#
#   cp config/agents.yaml.example config/agents.yaml
#
# Delete the file to go back to single-agent mode: the agent then uses the legacy
# paths (data/agent.db, reports/) and the models from .env — nothing changes.
#
# Per agent:
#   data/agents/<name>.db      state, memory, suggestions, cost
#   reports/<name>/<YYYY>/...  archived reports (+ its own index)
# and one email per agent, subject-tagged with the agent name.
#
# NAMES ARE PERMANENT-ISH: `name` becomes a database filename, a reports
# directory, and the subject tag on every email that agent sends. Renaming after
# the first run means moving files and splitting the report history, so pick
# names you can live with before you run. Name agents after the FILTER model
# (see below) — that's the thing that actually differs.
#
# `model` strings are OpenRouter model ids (https://openrouter.ai/models) when
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY is set. With `provider: anthropic` they are Anthropic model
# ids instead, so you can keep one agent on the direct Anthropic API.
#
# A leading `~` (e.g. `~anthropic/claude-haiku-latest`) is OpenRouter's alias
# routing — it resolves to the current model behind that alias. It is safe in
# YAML despite looking odd: a bare `~` means null only when it is the entire
# value, not when it prefixes a string. Pinned ids like the ones below are more
# reproducible; aliases keep you current. Pick per your taste.

# --- EXPERIMENT DESIGN — read this before adding agents ----------------------
#
# Two models per agent, and they are NOT equally important:
#
#   model          the FILTER. Scores every ingested item — hundreds of calls a
#                  run — and decides what appears in the report at all. This is
#                  where nearly all the cost and all the interesting behaviour
#                  lives.
#   summary_model  writes the report intro. Two or three sentences, twice a
#                  week. Rounding error, in both cost and influence.
#
# So vary ONE of them. Below, `summary_model` is identical for every agent and
# only the filter differs. Vary both and a better-looking report is ambiguous:
# did that agent select better items, or just write nicer prose about the same
# ones? Holding the summary constant means every difference you see between two
# reports comes from item selection.
#
# THE CONTROL PAIR: `haiku` and `haiku-control` run the same filter model on
# purpose. Scoring is not perfectly repeatable — even at temperature 0, batching,
# provider-side routing and each agent's own accumulated memory make two runs of
# one model disagree on some borderline items. That pair measures how much: the
# noise floor. A difference between two DIFFERENT models only means something
# once it exceeds that floor, and the pair's agreement is the practical ceiling
# for kappa, since no two models should agree more than a model agrees with
# itself. It looks like a redundant agent and it is the opposite — without it
# you cannot tell a real finding from sampling noise. Keep it.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

agents:
  - name: haiku
    # Cheap/fast filter model — used for relevance, memory, vetting, race results.
    model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5
    # Stronger model for writing the report intro. Defaults to `model` if
    # omitted. Held constant across the fleet — see EXPERIMENT DESIGN above.
    summary_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6
    enabled: true
    # The primary agent decides which agent's "already fetched" state gates
    # article downloads. Exactly one agent should be primary; the first enabled
    # agent is used if none is marked.
    primary: true

  - name: haiku-control
    # Intentional duplicate of `haiku`. Its disagreement with `haiku` is the
    # noise floor, not a finding. Delete it and the comparison loses its
    # yardstick.
    model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5
    summary_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6
    enabled: true

  # Prefer filters from DIFFERENT model families. Models from one family share
  # training data and tend to agree with each other, so a fleet of near-siblings
  # will look more unanimous than it deserves to.
  - name: gemini-flash
    model: google/gemini-2.5-flash
    summary_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6
    enabled: true

  - name: gpt5-mini
    model: openai/gpt-5-mini
    summary_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6
    enabled: true

  # Disabled agents are skipped entirely (no cost). Handy for parking a model
  # without deleting its history.
  - name: qwen
    model: qwen/qwen3-max
    summary_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6
    enabled: false
